# Shell scripts run on Linux CI runners (GitHub Actions) — must stay LF
# regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting, or the runner
# sees "$'\r': command not found" / bad-interpreter failures.
*.sh text eol=lf
# PowerShell scripts are Windows-first tooling — CRLF is the natural
# convention there, and Windows PowerShell tolerates LF fine either way,
# but CRLF keeps diffs clean for anyone editing them in a Windows editor.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
